    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "20. Strategic Reserves",
    "ruleNumber": "20.01",
    "summary": "When declaring battle formations, you can put any number of your units, except **FORTIFICATIONS**, into strategic reserves (also called Reserves). They are set aside instead of deployed and enter play later.\n\n- Unless a rule says otherwise, your strategic reserves units may total at most 50% of your battle size's points limit, counting units embarked in **TRANSPORTS** that are themselves in reserves.\n- Units still in strategic reserves when the final turn ends are destroyed, but their destruction triggers no rules.",
